  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR splits two long tests of the release tier into smaller tests. The tests do not share mutable state, so libtest runs them in parallel. Only test code changes.\n\n1. `crates/app/tests/rotary_field_parity.rs`: the test `every_rotary_kind_reads_the_radial_law_and_its_cost_is_measured` (768 s in release at the v0.20.0 cut) becomes 6 tests. Each test runs one `parity(Kind::X)` or one `eye_cost(Kind::X)` call:\n   - `the_parallel_kind_reads_the_radial_law`\n   - `the_contour_kind_reads_the_radial_law`\n   - `the_offset_kind_reads_the_radial_law`\n   - `the_parallel_kinds_eye_cost_is_measured`\n   - `the_contour_kinds_eye_cost_is_measured`\n   - `the_offset_kinds_eye_cost_is_measured`\n\n   The `parity` and `eye_cost` bodies do not change, so every assert stays. Each new test keeps `#[ignore]` with the lane name `heavy lane (M13.1 rotary parity)`.\n2. `crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement.rs`: the test `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name` (90 s in debug, a serial loop over 14 STEP files) becomes one test for each file (a `per_file!` macro), plus the file-set test. The file-set test keeps the old name. It asserts that the STEP files on disk are the `ROWS` files, in the same order, and that each row has its own test. A file with no row still fails the bench. Each file test compares its import verdict and its mesh verdict with its pinned row. The `ROWS` table and the verdict text do not change.\n\n## `#[test]` count\n\n| File | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `crates/app/tests/rotary_field_parity.rs` | 4 (1 ignored) | 9 (6 ignored) |\n| `crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement.rs` | 1 | 15 |\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-kernel --test step_agreement`: 15 passed, `finished in 9.29s` (before: about 90 s).\n- `cargo test --release -p camcraft-app --test rotary_field_parity -- --include-ignored` for the 3 not-ignored tests, the 3 eye-cost tests and `the_parallel_kind_reads_the_radial_law`: 7 passed, `finished in 196.70s` in parallel.\n\n## What was not run\n\n- `the_contour_kind_reads_the_radial_law` and `the_offset_kind_reads_the_radial_law` (release heavy lane, several minutes each). Their bodies are the same `parity()` calls as before.\n- clippy on the touched test files. The full quick gate.\n\n## Work that remains (issue 1715)\n\n- `the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_the_3d_finish` in `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies.rs` (about 28 min in release) is not split. It is one 3D Finish generate and one verify over the whole model. A split by level band changes what the test verifies (a band-by-band program is not the whole program), so it needs a decision about the fixture. It stays for the next PR.\n- `whole_model_pocket`, `keep_law`, `level_links`, `lathe_field_sim` are not split here.\n- The per-test time in the gate summary needs `xtask/`, which PR 1704 and issue 1714 own.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #1715\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
